    "reasoning": "Fourteen fields have mathematically correct answers supported by their own captured worked solutions. q-130523: matrix multiplication gives 10x+25y=15 and 12x+3y=-6; dividing the rows by 5 and 3 gives option 2. q-130528: the rows give 5y=9 and x=-1. q-73531: only III is closed and avoids the discontinuity at x=1; the solution's reference to [-1,1] while discussing [-2,2] is an interval typo that does not change the answer. q-129218: the domain is x>-2 with x≠2, so only II qualifies. q-69966: rationalization gives 4/5-8i/5, magnitude 4√5/5, and argument 2π-arctan(2), rounded to 5.176. q-19067 and q-73510 follow the product and chain rules; the latter derivative applies on 4<x<6. q-17339: cosine equals √3/2 at 30° and 330° modulo 360°, equivalently ±π/6 modulo 2π. q-87827: division by the negative logarithm ln(2/3) reverses the inequality. q-87855: collecting logarithms gives x ln(42)≥ln(7/9). q-162239: the third roots are 1 and -1/2±√3 i/2, matching image option 0. q-216709: the highlighted ninth root has index 3, hence e^(2πi/3). q-12284: the inverse matrix in option 4 gives (x,y)=(-7,-19). q-32136: the inverse matrix in option 3 gives (x,y)=(-3/5,2/5). Two fields contain substantive notation errors under the authoritative literal problem text: q-70313 displays the fraction 7/4, whose value is 7/4, whereas MA treats it as the binomial coefficient and answers 35. q-113611 displays a fraction equation, whose missing value is 1/4, whereas MA applies Pascal's identity and answers the displayed expression (5/3). The intended binomial answers are valid if the fraction notation is repaired to binomial notation, but neither literal fraction problem has a correct current choice. No submitted grade or earlier answer is supplied; all MA answer evidence below comes from each question's own worked solution.",
